<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">God Save the King</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as God Save the Queen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">God Save the King, or God Save the Queen when the monarch is female, is the national anthem of the United Kingdom, first published in the 1740s. It served as the national anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a> until they adopted their own; in Australia it was replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/advance-australia-fair">Advance Australia Fair</a> in 1984 and retained as the royal anthem.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/god-save-the-king.jpg" alt="God Save the King" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:God_Save_the_King_(sheet,_1745).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
